      "content": "While higher density generally requires less land and supports better transit use, claiming it is definitively \"better\" involves balancing environmental benefits against other social costs. The argument that single-family zoning is solely about property values overlooks the desire for neighborhood stability and specific lifestyles many residents value. Current urbanism trends suggest a shift towards mixed-use, adaptable zoning rather than a purely binary choice between the two extremes.",
      "source": "target",
